# Line endings are LF everywhere: in the repository, and in the working tree on
# every platform. Without this rule Git's `core.autocrlf` decides, and it is on
# by default on Windows and on the windows-latest CI runner, so a checkout there
# rewrites every text file to CRLF. That breaks two things at once: Prettier
# reports a formatting failure on 267 files, since `endOfLine: "lf"` is its
# default and `.editorconfig` asks for the same, and the tests that read this
# project's own source back and match it line by line stop matching.
#
# Nothing here is a workaround for the tool itself, which normalises line
# endings when it hashes and when it parses frontmatter, so a course file that
# arrives with CRLF still syncs correctly.
* text=auto eol=lf

# `text=auto` calls a file binary when it finds a NUL byte in the first 8000,
# which is true of every binary committed so far but is still a guess. These
# extensions are binary whatever the guess says.
*.docx binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
*.ttf binary
